{
  "version": {
    "en-US": {
      "type": "appStoreVersionLocalizations",
      "id": "76eff643-e1b8-43b8-8d49-d4e2311cd571",
      "attributes": {
        "description": "Kodo lets you feel the heartbeats of different animals through your iPhone's vibrations and animation.\n\nA human heart beats about 70 times a minute. A sparrow's beats around 800 times, and an elephant's only about 20. Numbers like these are hard to imagine, but in the palm of your hand the difference is unmistakable.\n\n- A collection of heartbeats\nNine animals are laid out like specimens in a display case: human, sparrow, elephant, octopus, chicken, cat, dog, horse and mouse. Inside each outline, a red heart beats at its real pace.\n\n- Feel it through vibration\nChoose an animal and your iPhone pulses at its heart rate. Small animals beat fast, large ones slowly. Close your eyes and compare.\n\n- Heart rates that change\nSwitch a human between rest, exercise and sleep, or a horse between rest and full gallop, and the heart rate changes with it.\n\n- Heart monitor view\nSwitch to text view to see every animal's heartbeat at once as a moving ECG trace, like a hospital monitor.\n\nHeart rates are approximate.",
        "locale": "en-US",
        "keywords": "heart,rate,pulse,bpm,ECG,monitor,vibration,haptic,biology,science,elephant,sparrow,horse,mouse",
        "marketingUrl": "https://harumidiv.github.io/AppleStoreDevelopprSite/detail/kodo.html",
        "promotionalText": "Feel the heartbeat of a living creature in the palm of your hand.",
        "supportUrl": "https://harumidiv.github.io/AppleStoreDevelopprSite/",
        "whatsNew": "Added support for multiple languages."
      },
      "relationships": {
